{%- comment -%} Quality / assays (from mockup) {%- endcomment -%}
<!-- How we qualify a batch -->
  <section class="section section-soft" id="quality">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="center">
        <span class="eyebrow">Our testing methodology</span>
        <h2>How We Qualify a Batch</h2>
        <p class="lead">Before any lot is listed for sale, it passes seven independent assays. Here is what each one actually checks — in plain English.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="assay-list">
        <div class="assay">
          <h3>Identity <span class="code">· LC-MS</span></h3>
          <p>Confirms the molecule in the vial is the molecule on the label, by matching its mass fingerprint against a reference standard.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="assay">
          <h3>Purity <span class="code">· HPLC-UV</span></h3>
          <p>Measures how much of the vial is the target compound versus related impurities. Our floor is 99% — anything below never ships.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="assay">
          <h3>Endotoxin <span class="code">· USP &lt;85&gt;</span></h3>
          <p>Screens for bacterial endotoxins that have no place in a clean research environment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="assay">
          <h3>Sterility <span class="code">· USP &lt;71&gt;</span></h3>
          <p>Verifies the sealed vial is free of microbial contamination before it ever leaves our facility.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="assay">
          <h3>Heavy Metals <span class="code">· ICP-MS</span></h3>
          <p>Tests for trace metals — lead, arsenic, mercury, cadmium — down to parts per billion.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="assay">
          <h3>Net Content</h3>
          <p>Confirms the actual peptide mass in the vial matches what is printed on the label. No underfilled vials.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="assay">
          <h3>Batch Consistency</h3>
          <p>Every new lot is compared against the original reference standard, so results stay reproducible from one order to the next.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="center mt-2">
        <p class="lead" style="font-size:1rem;">Every COA is published on the product page <strong>before</strong> the batch goes on sale — with the lab name, batch number, and test date.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
{% schema %}
{ "name": "Quality / assays", "settings": [] }
{% endschema %}
